        "mission_intent": "We need a full specification for the Design Definition process security engineering activities on the NextGen Federal Health Records platform, aligned with NIST SP 800-160 Volume 1 guidance. The spec must detail how security-related data and architectural constraints flow from the Architecture Definition process into the design phase, ensuring that system element designs remain consistent with the security architectural entities, models, and views established during architecture definition. It should explicitly address how the design process will eliminate, minimize, or contain design-level vulnerabilities and susceptibilities to disruption, hazards, and threats, including a taxonomy of design vulnerability categories relevant to our platform. The specification needs to preserve design-agnosticism from the architecture level while clearly articulating where architecture-level security concerns impose mandatory constraints on the design trade space\u2014document each such constraint with traceability back to the originating requirement or stakeholder concern and the viewpoint analysis that vetted it. Include a feedback mechanism specification describing how security design constraints and findings feed back into Architecture Definition to confirm proper allocation of security properties and to validate that emergent system properties, including but not limited to security, are achievable. Deliverable is due to the Systems Engineering Review Board by end of next sprint, with all constraint traceability matrices populated and peer-reviewed by at least two security engineers from the architecture team.",
